mindmap
  root((GitHub Copilot\nCustomization))
    Instruction Levels
      Organization
        Set in GitHub org settings
        Applies to all members on GitHub.com
        Use for coding standards, security, tone
      Personal
        Set under your profile on GitHub.com
        Only applies to you
        Good for personal testing
      Repository-Wide
        .github/copilot-instructions.md
        Always-on for every chat request
        Works across all IDEs and GitHub.com
        Use for team conventions and project standards
      Path-Specific
        NAME.instructions.md in .github/instructions/
        Applied via applyTo glob patterns
        Use for language or directory-specific rules
        Not supported in JetBrains / Xcode / mobile
    Reusable Task Files
      Prompt Files
        .github/prompts/*.prompt.md
        On-demand, must be explicitly invoked
        Supports dynamic input variables
        Frontmatter mode: ask / edit / agent
        VS Code, Visual Studio, JetBrains only
      Agent Skills
        skills/skill-name/SKILL.md
        Auto-invoked by intent matching
        Reusable shareable expertise
        Supported in Claude Code, VS Code, JetBrains
        No dynamic variables or mode control
    Agents
      Custom Agents
        .github/agents/*.agent.md
        Sustains configuration across full workflow
        Define persona, scope, tool access
        Supports model preference and handoffs
        GitHub cloud and VS Code local agents
      AGENTS.md
        Plain Markdown, no schema required
        README for agents: build, test, conventions
        Open standard under Linux Foundation
        Supported by 20+ coding tools
      Agent Plugins
        Bundled slash commands, skills, agents, MCP
        Installed from VS Code marketplace
        Currently in preview
    Hard Limits
      4000 chars max for PR code review per file
      ~1000 lines soft limit before degradation
      No external URL fetching in instructions
      Inline autocomplete NOT affected
      PR review uses base branch only
    Best Practices
      Start with 10-20 instructions, iterate
      Keep tool lists minimal in agents
      Separate planning from implementation agents
      Define explicit scope limits
      Avoid conflicting instructions across files
      Split repo-wide vs path-specific concerns
